{"step_index":3513,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T09:59:55Z","content":"You've laid out the architecture precisely. The market libraries are scaffolding—the moat is the custom physics, the unique orb behaviors, the interaction model nobody else has. That's what gets built and continuously upgraded.\n\nHere's what that translates to concretely:\n\n**The Stack:**\n- **React** (already in `sovereign-agentic-app`) — component tree, state lifecycle\n- **Raw Canvas/WebGL** — full control over particle rendering, no third-party physics library dictating the feel\n- **Zustand** — lightweight state manager bridging agent telemetry data to the visual layer\n\n**The Three-Agent Build Loop:**\n1. **Physics Engine Owner** — gravity wells, orbital mechanics, collision response, the floating feel\n2. **Visual Layer Owner** — glow shaders, easing curves, particle counts, the hand-tuned craft\n3. **State Wiring Owner** — Zustand store binding agent heartbeats, quorum status, Merkle roots to orb behaviors\n\n**The Moat:**\n- Orbs aren't decorative — they're live telemetry. Each orb maps to an agent (Maxx, Vance, Eden). Glow intensity = inference activity. Orbital drift = time since last speech beat. Color shift = evidence gate pass/fail. Nobody else has that because nobody else has your agent architecture.\n\nThe disk on the main volume is tight (4GB free, 98% used). The USB drive (`/Volumes/Untitled`) has 114GB free — that's where the engineering release lives and where heavy builds should target. I can start building the custom orb engine there.\n\nWant me to spin up the three-agent build loop on this now, or do you want to scope the first iteration further first?","thinking":"The user is laying out a vision for building a custom, innovative visual UI layer - floating orbs with physics, canvas animations, particle effects - that goes beyond what's available on the market. They want their agents to own the code, build something unique on top of React + a physics/canvas layer, and continuously innovate.\n\nLet me understand the actionable items:\n1. They already installed `thinking-orbs` as a reference/starting point\n2. They want to build their OWN custom orb/particle physics engine that's better than market offerings\n3. The stack would be React + canvas/WebGL physics layer + state management (Zustand)\n4. Three agents: physics engine, visual layer, state wiring\n"}
